Rebuild procedure
-----------------

The preferred rebuild path is the manually dispatched
`.github/workflows/rebuild-windows-sfx.yml` workflow. It verifies both outputs
and uploads an artifact containing the two executables, SHA256SUMS.txt, and
BUILDINFO.json. GitHub's build-provenance attestation is published separately
by the same run. The workflow has read-only repository access and never commits
the generated files.

After downloading the artifact, verify SHA256SUMS.txt before manually replacing
both checked-in SFX files. SHA256SUMS.txt and BUILDINFO.json are provenance
sidecars rather than Firefox packaging inputs, so they are not copied by
setup.sh or stored in this overlay directory; preserve them with the release
records. Update the current build-info block above whenever the executables
are replaced.

The workflow pins Windows SDK 10.0.22621.0 because the project's v142 ARM64
compiler is incompatible with the newer 10.0.26100.0 headers selected by an
unqualified `WindowsTargetPlatformVersion=10.0`.

For an equivalent local rebuild:

1. Check out Firefox commit
   `0c39e9282688363f5028d0541c17784f7fa5117c` in a clean tree. There is no need
   to run the full Mercury setup.sh solely to rebuild these files.
2. Apply `patches/firefox-153/170-mercury-windows-sfx-branding.patch` to the
   Firefox checkout and copy this directory's setup.ico over Firefox's
   `other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/setup.ico`.
3. Install Visual Studio 2022 with the MSVC v142 x86/x64 and ARM64 build tools
   plus Windows SDK 10.0.22621.0. Do not retarget the project to an unrecorded
   toolset or SDK when matching the checked-in build configuration.
4. Build both ReleaseD targets from the Firefox checkout:

       msbuild other-licenses\7zstub\firefox\SFXSetup.sln /m /t:Rebuild /p:Configuration=ReleaseD /p:Platform=x86 /p:WindowsTargetPlatformVersion=10.0.22621.0
       msbuild other-licenses\7zstub\firefox\SFXSetup.sln /m /t:Rebuild /p:Configuration=ReleaseD /p:Platform=ARM64 /p:WindowsTargetPlatformVersion=10.0.22621.0

5. Replace 7zSD.Win32.sfx with `Win32\ReleaseD\7zSD.Win32.sfx` and replace
   7zSD.ARM64.sfx with `ARM64\ReleaseD\7zSD.ARM64.sfx`.
6. Verify both files' SHA-256 hashes, PE machine types, version resources,
   embedded icons, and Windows 10 minimum-version messages. Then build and
   launch each corresponding Windows installer.

Regenerate both executables whenever Firefox changes any file under
other-licenses/7zstub, even if Firefox does not update its checked-in binaries
in the same commit.
